course: dictionary
lesson: 13557
title: Pure and impure
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Something is pure when it is made of only one thing, with nothing mixed in. Something is impure when other substances are mixed in with it. «The water from the pond was impure, full of mud and leaves.» The mud and leaves are mixed into the water, so it is not clean.
explain: An impurity is the bit that should not be there. Impure is the describing word, and impurity is the naming word. «The sand is an impurity in the sugar» tells you the sand spoils the sugar.
explain: Scientists clean impure substances to make them pure again. They can filter out solid bits, or evaporate water to leave the salt behind. When you read a sentence about mixing, ask yourself: is something spoiled by other things mixed in?
explain: Old religious rules used impure in a different way, to mean spiritually unclean. In science, use the everyday meaning: mixed with other substances.
fact: Impure means mixed with other substances, so not pure or clean.
fact: «Impure» can describe water, metal or a sample: «an impure sample».
fact: An impurity is a substance that makes something less pure.
fact: Filtering, evaporating and distilling are ways to remove impurities.
fact: In old religious rules, impure meant spiritually unclean, not just dirty.
exercise: «The river water was impure, so we boiled it before drinking.» What does impure mean here? | Made of only one thing | *Mixed with other substances, not clean | Shiny and clear | Very cold
exercise: Which word means the bit that spoils a pure substance? | *Impurity | Distillation | Evaporation | Purity
exercise: «The gold bar was impure, so it was not worth as much.» Which word means the opposite of impure? | Heavy | *Pure | Dirty | Mixed
test: Which process turns water into vapour and leaves the salt behind? | *Evaporating | Freezing | Mixing | Filtering
test: «The old rules called the food impure.» In this old religious sense, what does impure mean? | *Morally or spiritually unclean, as in old rules of worship | Very tasty | Made of only one thing | Full of light
exam: Which sentence uses impure correctly? | The cake was pure, so it was very hot. | The bell rang loudly across the school. | The sky was impure, because it was blue. | *The gold bar was impure, with other metals mixed into it.
